      "text_unit_id": "tu_0001",
      "verbatim_text": "Wall thickness ≥14 mm in one or more LV myocardial segments not sufficiently explained solely by abnormal loading conditions. LVOTO ≥30 mmHg at rest or exercise, asymmetric hypertrophy, or increased LGE in a patchy mid-wall pattern in the most hypertrophied segment, further suggest the presence of HCM. It can be considered familial when two or more first- or second-degree relatives with HCM or a first-degree relative with autopsy proven HCM and sudden death at <50 years of age are detected."
    },
