      "text_unit_id": "tu_0004",
      "verbatim_text": "With LVOTO Avoid hypovolaemia (dehydration), arterial and venous dilators (nitrates and phosphodiesterase type 5 inhibitors), and digoxin. Use non-vasodilating beta-blockers or use verapamil if beta-blockers non-tolerated or ineffective. Low-dose loop or thiazide diuretics must be used with caution to improve dyspnoea associated with LVOTO, but avoiding hypovolaemia. Invasive treatment (septal reduction therapy by alcohol ablation or myomectomy), in experienced centres, may be considered in those patients with a resting or maximum provoked LVOT ≥50 mmHg and/or who remain symptomatic (NYHA class III or IV, syncope) despite OMT. Novel drugs or devices may be considered once available. 909,927"
    }
